@@ -401,3 +401,15 @@ The account provider’s `embeddedPageDist` configuration adds a `dist` query pa
 ## Dev Note
 
 Pre-launch CDN and capacity decisions are tracked in the [Desktop update proposal](../../.agents/notes/proposed/feature/2026-09-08-desktop-update-policy-and-installation.md#cdn-and-capacity-qualification).
+
+
+## Authorized delivery snapshots (validation patch)
+
+The `dshDesktop.sessionFileActions` main-frame bridge serves the matching Session File Actions plugin. `begin(operationId)` accepts a new copy and immediately revokes any earlier preparation, even if the new Host authorization later fails. `copy` consumes that reservation once and redeems a short-lived, one-use Host grant through the private fixed endpoint; renderer paths, URLs and bytes are never accepted as file authority. The Host re-resolves the session delivery and checks file permissions at execution.
+
+`cancel` affects preparation only. Publication cannot be cancelled once submitted. The shared snapshot module validates its bytes and file name before publishing `ClipboardItem` `text/uri-list`. Pending files are removed on failure/cancellation; published or uncertain references survive unload and application exit. No automatic reclamation is implemented in this validation patch. Full-file reads currently use the Host's 32 MiB bound and report `too_large`; larger-file support remains a release validation item.
+
+Safe diagnostics contain operation ID, stage, classified reason and known errno, never raw paths or file bodies. `copied` requires the clipboard write promise to succeed; an uncertain publication returns `unconfirmed`. Rebuild using the repository `build:artifacts` then `build:check`; regressions live in `tests/session-file-actions.spec.ts`.
+
+
+`begin` returns a boolean receipt: `true` is the sole acceptance/supersession boundary; `false` means a previous copy is still publishing and preserves that operation. The client cancels older authorization only after acceptance, and always processes main-owned copied/unconfirmed receipts independently from authorization cancellation.
